<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="api_player_pause_player">
    <title><ph keyref="Pause_Player"/></title>
    <shortdesc id="short"><ph id="shortdesc" props="cpp">Pauses playback.</ph><ph id="shortdesc" props="android">Pauses playback.</ph><ph id="shortdesc" props="ios mac">Pauses the playback.</ph></shortdesc>
    <prolog>
        <metadata>
            <keywords>
                <indexterm keyref="Pause_Player"/>
            </keywords>
        </metadata>
    </prolog>
    <refbody>
        <section id="prototype">
            <p outputclass="codeblock">
                <codeblock props="cpp" outputclass="language-cpp">bool Pause(Error *err = nullptr)</codeblock>
                <codeblock props="android" outputclass="language-java">public void pause() throws RteException</codeblock>
            <codeblock props="ios mac" outputclass="language-objectivec">- (BOOL)pause:(AgoraRteError * _Nullable)error;</codeblock>
            </p>
        </section>
        <section id="detailed_desc" deliveryTarget="details" otherprops="no-title">
            <dl outputclass="since">
                <dlentry props="cpp">
                    <dt>Since</dt>
                    <dd>Added since version v4.4.0.</dd>
                </dlentry>
                <dlentry props="android">
                    <dt>Since</dt>
                    <dd>Available since v4.4.0.</dd>
                </dlentry>
            <dlentry props="ios mac">
                <dt>Since</dt>
                <dd>v4.5.0</dd>
            </dlentry>
            </dl>
            <p props="cpp">After calling <xref keyref="Play_Player"/> to play a URL resource, you can call this method to pause playback. If you need to stop playback, call the <xref keyref="Stop_Player"/> method.</p>
            <p props="android">After calling <xref keyref="Play_Player"/> to play a URL resource, you can call this method to pause playback. To stop playback, call <xref keyref="Stop_Player"/>.</p>
        <p props="ios mac">When you call <xref keyref="Play_Player"/> to play a URL, if you want to pause the playback, you can call this method. If you need to stop the playback, call <xref keyref="Stop_Player"/>.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="timing" deliveryTarget="details" props="android cpp">
            <title>Timing</title>
            <p props="cpp">This method must be called after <xref keyref="Play_Player"/>.</p>
            <p props="android">You must call this method after calling <xref keyref="Play_Player"/>.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="related" deliveryTarget="details" props="android cpp">
            <title>Related Callbacks</title>
            <p props="cpp">After successfully calling this method, the SDK triggers the <xref keyref="onStateChanged"/> callback reporting the player state as <codeph>kRtePlayerStatePaused</codeph>.</p>
            <p props="android">After successfully calling this method, the <xref keyref="onStateChanged"/> callback is triggered to report the player status as <codeph>PAUSED</codeph>.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="parameters" deliveryTarget="details" props="cpp ios mac">
            <title>Parameters</title>
            <parml>
                <plentry props="cpp">
                    <pt>err</pt>
                    <pd>Output parameter, status or error information. See <xref keyref="Error"/>.</pd>
                </plentry>
            <plentry conkeyref="SetConfigs_Rte/err" props="ios mac">
                <pt/>
                <pd/>
            </plentry>
            </parml>
        </section>
        <section id="exception" props="android">
            <title>Exceptions</title>
            <p props="android">When this method call fails, the SDK throws an <xref keyref="RteException"/> with the corresponding error information. You need to catch and handle the exception.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="return_values" props="cpp ios mac">
            <title>Return Values</title>
            <p props="cpp">
                <ul>
                    <li><xref keyref="true"/>: Playback paused successfully.</li>
                    <li><xref keyref="false"/>: Failed to pause playback.</li>
                </ul>
            </p>
        <p props="ios mac">Whether the playback has been successfully paused:<ul>
                <li><codeph><ph keyref="true"/></codeph>: The playback is paused.</li>
                <li><codeph><ph keyref="false"/></codeph>: Pausing the playback fails.</li>
                </ul>
            </p> </section>
    </refbody>
</reference>
